== Origin

This add-on is based on the Balboa binding written by Carl Önnheim in 2020
(https://github.com/carlonnheim/openhab-addons/tree/balboa).

ddempsey3 updated that binding for openHAB 3.0 in December 2020
(https://github.com/ddempsey3/openhab-addons/tree/balboa-3). This add-on continues from that version: it was ported
to openHAB 5.2 and extended by Larsen-Locke.

Thomas Binder (binderth, https://github.com/binderth) contributed the fix for the lock-order deadlocks between the
protocol, its writer and the reconnect job, and the clock, spa state, notification, hold, circulation and filter
cycle channels (release 5.2.1.7).

The original binding was released under the Eclipse Public License 2.0, and so is this add-on. The license headers of
the source files are kept as they are.

== Protocol Documentation

Balboa does not publish the protocol of its Wi-Fi module. The message layouts of the fault log and the filter cycles
are taken from the community protocol documentation at https://github.com/ccutrer/balboa_worldwide_app
(doc/protocol.md). The decoding of the system information, the setup parameters, the Wi-Fi module identification
and the further status fields follows pybalboa (https://github.com/garbled1/pybalboa).
